WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.860
I have to pinch myself that I am saying&nbsp;
but, but here goes. Today we are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:18.720
use Google’s amazing new AI to create not an&nbsp;
image, and not even a short image sequence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.700
but we are going to make an entire film. An&nbsp;
AI-made film, and all this within seconds.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:35.580
Yes, that’s right. Less than a year ago, in&nbsp;
April 2022, an amazing text to image AI called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.340
DALL-E 2 was published by scientists&nbsp;
at OpenAI. This took a piece of text,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:48.480
and painted an image for us. It ushered&nbsp;
in a new era of AI-assisted tools.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:57.540
And then, something amazing happened. And not&nbsp;
6 years later, but about only 6 months later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:03.300
in October 2022. This follow up&nbsp;
paper could generate not just images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.180
but short videos of our choosing,&nbsp;
but even if it did that really well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:16.620
this was still made to create only that…short&nbsp;
sequences. A true miracle of AI research.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.960
However, here is another one. And&nbsp;
hold on to your papers, because now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:30.780
this new technique called Phenaki promises no&nbsp;
less than entire films made by an AI. Entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:38.760
films! Now I am super excited for this, so let’s&nbsp;
have a look at 5 of my favorite examples together.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.640
One. The new work’s superpower is that&nbsp;
we can write several text prompts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:51.600
and the AI finds a way to chain them together in&nbsp;
a way that makes sense. That sounds…that sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:58.380
exactly like the script for a movie.&nbsp;
Amazing. If it works, of course. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:06.180
first, we can say “A photorealistic teddy bear&nbsp;
is swimming in the ocean in San Francisco.” Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:13.080
we say “The teddy bear goes underwater.” Then,&nbsp;
“The teddy bear keeps swimming under the water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:19.920
with colorful fishes.” And finally,&nbsp;
“A panda bear is swimming underwater.”

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:26.820
And the AI finds out by itself how this&nbsp;
magical transformation from teddy bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:34.980
to a panda should take place. I love it. Now,&nbsp;
this was really cool, how about another one?

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:43.140
Two. We start out with a side view of an astronaut&nbsp;
who is walking through a puddle on Mars. Who then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:50.280
starts dancing. I am particularly interested in&nbsp;
these transitionary moments, this one checks out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:59.580
really cool. Then, he walks his dog on Mars. And&nbsp;
look at that! The dog does not seem to just grow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:06.960
out of nothing, but it gradually enters the frame.&nbsp;
Once again, a graceful transition. And then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:12.960
the astronaut and this good boy watch&nbsp;
fireworks together. Well, kind of.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:19.680
Three, I also loved that we can also give&nbsp;
the AI a little more explicit instructions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.720
for instance, we can ask it to zoom&nbsp;
out at the end of the video when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:30.660
the campfire appears. And it did&nbsp;
exactly that. Good job, little AI!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:38.340
Four, the paper also showcases a two and a&nbsp;
half minute long video that starts out with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.980
a scenic motorcycle ride, running through&nbsp;
the woods and finding beautiful things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.020
of course, robots, and more.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:55.860
And five, while we look through the beautiful&nbsp;
story of this penguin, let’s talk about pixels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:05.940
These are 128x128 videos. That is not a lot&nbsp;
of pixels. Now, of course, these are not super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:12.600
high-quality videos yet, they do not compare to&nbsp;
the super-high quality images that text to image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:20.760
AIs are capable of. So why be so excited for this?&nbsp;
Well, we are experienced Fellow Scholars here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:29.940
so what do we do? We apply the First Law of&nbsp;
Papers. The First Law Of Papers says that research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:36.660
is a process. Do not look at where we are, look&nbsp;
at where we will be two more papers down the line.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.000
So, where will we be a couple more papers&nbsp;
down the line? Well, for reference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.820
this is what DALL-E 1 was capable of,&nbsp;
and just one more paper down the line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:54.540
this was possible with DALL-E 2. And looking&nbsp;
at the previous results in image generation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.540 --> 00:05:02.460
we are likely having a DALL-E 1 moment for AI&nbsp;
video generation. Yes, this means we are likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:10.740
on the cusp of a revolution. Just look at how much&nbsp;
progress can be made in just one paper. Wow. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:17.940
high-quality AI movies are likely not&nbsp;
impossible anymore. And not even decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:23.640
away. They might very well be just months&nbsp;
away from now. What a time to be alive!

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:30.120
And, if you wish to be part of this amazing&nbsp;
progress in AI research, consider subscribing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:36.060
and becoming a Fellow Scholar, and even&nbsp;
better, hitting the bell icon to not miss it.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:43.920
Now, plus one, this has become one of my favorite&nbsp;
parts of the paper. Get this, it can even animate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:51.600
an already existing image of ours given a text&nbsp;
prompt. So, we can not only create entire movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:59.220
but we can even tell the AI what kind of&nbsp;
movie we wish to create. Wow. My goodness.

